[*] GTKWave save file for tb_compare: Harvard vs shared memory on the same program.
[*] Look for an LW/SW: on Harvard, i_addr and d_addr are both active in ONE cycle
[*] (h d_we/d_re high); on the baseline, m_addr carries the PC, then the data address
[*] in the next cycle (m_is_data = 1), so the same instruction takes two cycles.
